    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389-a5">

                <pb facs="0917" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg821"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 1002.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Ruelas.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 25,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I respectfully request your excellency to
                    issue a letter of matriculation to Mr. Blanchard B. Kelly, resident in this
                    city, who is registered in the consulate-general in <pb facs="0918" n="822"
                        xml:id="pg822"/> this city as a citizen of the United States, and recognized
                    by this legation as entitled to all the rights and privileges as such, upon the
                    faith of the passport of the Secretary of State inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>With a renewed expression of my high esteem, I remain your excellency’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
